widowed by the 9 11 attacks  former member of the last man battalion  former joint task force head of  department  conspiracy theorist genius tech  entrepreneur  why was this anti-government anti-shd  civilian so important to the success of  the division's mission  in new york city  born and raised in central jersey he  attended rutgers university  and was later involved in a number of  tech startups  a highly anxious and cynical individual  rhodes was the type of person who never  liked to dwell in any place for too long  he felt like an outsider wherever he  went and could never find a good enough  reason to stay  it's a surprise that he managed to stay  in manhattan long enough to meet his  wife  perhaps she pretended not to be  interested and rhodes who isn't afraid  to knuckle down when the going gets  tough  was intrigued unfortunately  not long after they wed the 9 11 attacks  occurred  and she was one of the people killed in  the world trade center north tower  collapse  utterly devastated road sought revenge  against the terrorists he was furious at  the us government's response  and because of this rather than joining  the u.s armed forces  he joined a private military company  called the last man battalion  in 2003 the lmb was stationed in iraq  and rhodes was serving his time as an  engineering contractor  not long after they were stationed his  team was ambushed  and the attack left him as the sole  survivor of his unit  overcome with feelings of guilt he was  constantly questioning why he had  escaped death  while others had lost their lives again  and again  he wondered whether it was something he  could have done to prevent the ambush or  in some way that he could have saved the  others lives  eventually the strain of survivor's  guilt proved too much  even for him and rhodes left iraq and  the lnb  returning to manhattan this event  paired with losing his wife meant that  rhodes does the utmost to avoid any kind  of intimate relationships with others  he has a lingering distrust of most  government agencies including the  division  and his time working with the last man  battalion has only further enhanced his  skeptical  and blunt outlook according to the  division's personnel  vials rhodes is considered to be  incredibly intelligent  a tech genius and an expert weapons  engineer  above all else he places the highest of  value on an individual's capability on  doing what is right  for the greater good  after the dollar flu outbreak rhodes  offered his services to the joint task  force  in new york he quickly rose through the  ranks to become the chief engineer  after a power outage in the jtf base of  operations  rhodes traced the fault back to a  generator failure in the subway morgue  while leading a team down to fix the  fault the jtf suddenly lost contact with  them  second wave division agents staged a  rescue mission  in turn allowing him to restore power to  the base of operations  later an lmb member and a friend of his  from way back when they worked together  decided to defect from the private  military company stating that he didn't  support the direction that they were  heading  so rhodes sent in a small jtf team to  extract him in exchange for l b  intel unfortunately the lmb found out  they sent a squad to kill rhodes team  and the traitor  reluctantly rhodes asked the division to  assist him in rescuing his friend  they were successful and managed to  deliver the lmb deserter to a jtf squad  who are waiting to take him back  to the base of operations  throughout the activities early on in  the outbreak rhodes continued to provide  expert advice  and advanced technical solutions towards  everything that the hostile factions  were able to throat them  i can't do this [ __ ] anymore it's  probably just a power outage  the network going down and you get in  orders to go to dc  which you ignored by the way is not just  a power outage  we all got the call it was probably just  a glitch in the system  i'm needed here you're not needed  anywhere  paul you know i don't trust the division  i can't  between keener and first wave [ __ ]  the network [ __ ] isaac  constant reminders that director 51 was  a terrible idea gone too far  so what do you want to do rhodes i want  you to stop  justifying the [ __ ] law and take  some goddamn responsibility  the months following the activation of  directive 51 saw poor decision  after poor decision including badly  planned quarantine zones  and then the portrayal of countless  numbers of division agents  rhodes needed people he could trust and  the division were not it  he needed out we need to talk  that's never good you're gonna need to  find a new lackey  you leaving rose benitez already told  you  he gave me a heads up he trusts me  i know it's been hard for you here you  haven't been happy for a long time  i've never been happy at least you're  honest you need me to train my  replacement or something we'll manage  go ahead you quit on us a long time ago  help  out your new settlement maybe you'll  find whatever it is you're looking for  whatever well  rhodes left the joint task force and the  base of operations  he went on to assist a number of  civilian settlements with their  preparations  and defenses eventually he established  his own settlement with a number of  former jtf  who had also had enough of the bad calls  coming from above  this settlement was called haven and was  located in southern manhattan  he would make sure that the community's  needs would be placed first  any outside help would be avoided if  possible he wasn't going to take any  chances with the care of the people  who looked to him for safety  hey agent rhodes is that you the hell  are you doing down here  finding a new way okay you gonna let me  in  sorry sorry you're not welcome here  oh come on rhodes these people count on  me to keep them safe  and i've seen you in the field i can't  let you in  have it your way roads you'll be sorry  i'm not here to protect you when rikers  come knocking on your door  okay take care now we'll handle the  rikers on our own thank you  however when the new york city hall was  attacked by the infamous rogue agent  aaron kina  it resulted in massive casualties to the  jtf and the division forces stationed  there  and although rhodes had a deep mistrust  of these agencies and had witnessed time  and time again the destruction that the  division agents brought along with them  he began to realize that the attacks  were inevitably getting closer and  closer to his new home  [ __ ] that the division had its chance we  need somewhere to regroup  find somewhere else how do you know  haven isn't keener's next target  are you kidding me you make us a target  we can keep you safe of course you can  just like hell's kitchen i'm not gonna  fall for that [ __ ] again  we're fighting this same fight here  you know what  our situation's a [ __ ] ton better than  ever was back in midtown  these people feel safe  you're right the situation  feels better for you now but feeling  safe  doesn't mean you are safe it's getting  pretty rough out deadpool  but it's your decision  do what you need to take care of keener  and then i want you out  all of you  so reluctantly rhodes allowed feylau and  the division to use haven as a forward  operating base in the hunt for aramkina  unsurprisingly he certainly didn't hold  back in expressing his distrust of them  and the superiors  he continued to help the division  throughout the southern manhattan  manhunt  in an attempt to have him leave haven as  soon as possible  after the division had caught up with  kina and eliminated him  it was discovered that feylau had gone  rogue and was working for the black tusk  rhodes had never trusted her and even  from early on they clashed  in his eyes this was the final nail in  the coffin for the division  though he appreciated what the division  had accomplished along with saving haven  in the process  his trust in the division would never be  restored  ever since the loss of his wife in the 9  11 attacks  rhodes has had a strong sense of disdain  for the government  so when he began to see the division  starting to fall apart with agents going  rogue  and his relationship with feylau going  from bad to worse  it's no surprise that he wanted to get  as far away as possible from it  [Music]  however with the virus rampant wards  raging across new york city  and the rest of the united states it was  only so long before haven would come  under threat  and rhodes would need to take action the  division needed his help  and he needed them too  rhodes is infused with a strong sense of  doing what is right  even when it comes to working with  others he mistrusts  and for this reason he's always been  there to assist the division  his intelligence ability with technology  and weapons  means that he's an invaluable source to  have at their disposal  and whom without the division would have  struggled to complete what they've  achieved so far  i hope you've enjoyed this thank you  very much for watching and i'll catch  you in the next one  [Music]  [Applause]  cheers  [Music]

